IMPORT prelude

-- Antitrust Guidelines for International Enforcement and Cooperation (U.S. Department of
-- Justice and Federal Trade Commission, 13 January 2017) -- THE NOUNS.
--
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW. The guidelines say how the two agencies will exercise
-- their enforcement discretion. "No set of guidelines could possibly indicate how the
-- Agencies will assess the particular facts of every case" (1 [pdf page 6]), and they "are
-- not intended to, do not, and may not be relied upon to create any rights, substantive or
-- procedural, enforceable at law by any party in any matter, civil or criminal" (1 [pdf
-- page 7]). Nothing here says what a court must hold.
--
-- Types only: no rules, no #EVAL. Every field is a fact the caller supplies. Many are
-- findings the guidelines leave to the agencies (whether an effect is "direct, substantial,
-- and reasonably foreseeable" is "a question of fact", 3.2 [pdf page 24]); those are inputs,
-- never computed, and each says so. A finding the text distinguishes as not yet made is a
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN: NOTHING is "not yet determined", JUST FALSE is "found not to be so"
-- (fork F8).
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/2017-international-enforcement-cooperation-guidelines.txt.
-- Section numbers are as printed; "[pdf page N]" is the page marker of that text.

§ `Antitrust Guidelines for International Enforcement and Cooperation (2017) -- the nouns`

§§ `2 Relevant antitrust and related statutes`

-- 2 [pdf page 7]: the two determinations after which "the Agencies apply the same
-- substantive rules to all cases". The parties' nationality is read by no rule: "The
-- Agencies do not discriminate in the enforcement of the antitrust laws based on the
-- nationality of the parties."
DECLARE `Determinations before the same substantive rules apply (2)` HAS
    `the agencies determine that a sufficient nexus to the United States exists to apply the antitrust laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agencies determine that neither international comity nor the involvement of a foreign jurisdiction precludes investigation or enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nationality of the parties` IS A STRING

-- 2.2 [pdf page 9]: the two prohibitions of Section 5 of the FTC Act.
DECLARE `Prohibition of Section 5 of the FTC Act (2.2)` IS ONE OF
    `the prohibition of unfair methods of competition`
    `the prohibition of unfair or deceptive acts or practices`

-- 2.4 [pdf page 11]. Whether a statute applies is a finding.
DECLARE `Transaction and the HSR Act (2.4)` HAS
    `the transaction is subject to the HSR Act's notification and waiting period requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Sherman Act, the FTC Act or the Clayton Act applies to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 2.7 [pdf pages 14-15]: the NCRPA's notification procedure, as the 2017 text summarises it.
DECLARE `Notified venture under the NCRPA (2.7)` HAS
    `the participants have provided notice to the agencies under the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the challenged conduct is within the scope of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the venture is a joint production venture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the principal facilities for such production are located in the United States or its territories` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each person who controls any party to the venture, the party included, is a United States person, or a foreign person from a country whose law accords antitrust treatment no less favorable to United States persons than to its domestic persons for participation in joint ventures for production` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 2.8 [pdf page 15]: an association seeking the Webb-Pomerene exemption.
DECLARE `Export association (2.8)` HAS
    `it is an association of otherwise competing businesses engaging collectively in export sales` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the exports are of goods, wares, or merchandise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct has an anticompetitive effect in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct injures domestic competitors of the members of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the association files its articles of agreement and annual reports with the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 2.9 [pdf page 16]: the four things an applicant for an export trade certificate of review
-- "must show that proposed export conduct will" do, in the text's order.
DECLARE `Showing by an applicant for an export trade certificate of review (2.9)` HAS
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will result in neither a substantial lessening of competition or restraint of trade within the United States nor a substantial restraint of the export trade of any competitor of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will not unreasonably enhance, stabilize, or depress prices in the United States of the class of goods or services covered by the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will not constitute unfair methods of competition against competitors engaged in the export of the class of goods or services exported by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will not include any act that may reasonably be expected to result in the sale for consumption or resale in the United States of such goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 2.9 [pdf pages 16-17]: conduct and a certificate that has been issued.
DECLARE `Conduct under an export trade certificate of review (2.9)` HAS
    `the person is named in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity is specified in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity complies with the terms of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate was obtained by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of Commerce or the Department determines that the export activities have ceased to comply with the statutory criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct threatens a clear and irreparable harm to the national interest` IS A BOOLEAN   -- a finding

-- 2.12 [pdf page 19]: an agreement settling a trade dispute.
DECLARE `Settlement of a trade dispute (2.12)` HAS
    `the agreement complies with the specific procedures in the U.S. trade laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement goes beyond the measures authorized by such laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the settlement involves price and quantity agreements or otherwise implicates the antitrust laws` IS A BOOLEAN   -- read by no rule: immunity is granted "even if" it does

-- 2.12 [pdf page 19]: officials' part in measures that would otherwise violate the
-- antitrust laws.
DECLARE `Government officials and the measures (2.12)` HAS
    `there is legal authority for the measures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `U.S. or foreign government officials were involved in or encouraged the measures` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `3 Conduct involving foreign commerce`

-- 3.1 [pdf pages 22-23] and Illustrative Examples A to D [pdf pages 23-28]: the facts from
-- which the kind of commerce the conduct involves is read (fork F1 in NOTES.md). Four fields
-- are facts that 3.1 says do not decide it, read by no rule.
DECLARE `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` HAS
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Example A; Example B's second limb (sales to customers in the United States); Example C assumes not
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Example B
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.1: "the conduct being challenged must itself involve import commerce"; a finding, for a case the Examples do not show
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.1: not enough by itself
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.1: not needed
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.1: not needed
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.1, Example A: does not matter
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS A BOOLEAN   -- names the non-import kind: export, or else wholly foreign (3.2)
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN   -- n.80

-- 3.2 [pdf page 24]; Section 6a(1) as quoted at [pdf pages 20-21].
DECLARE `Kind of commerce the conduct involves (3)` IS ONE OF
    `commerce within the United States`
    `U.S. import commerce`
    `U.S. export commerce`
    `wholly foreign commerce`

-- Section 6a(1)(A) and (B) as quoted [pdf pages 20-21]; 3.2 [pdf page 24].
DECLARE `Commerce an effect is on (3.2)` IS ONE OF
    `trade or commerce within the United States`
    `U.S. import trade or commerce`
    `the export trade or commerce of a person engaged in such trade or commerce in the United States`

-- 3.2 [pdf pages 24-25, 28]: one effect of the conduct on U.S. commerce. Each finding is the
-- agencies' (a court's, in a private action): NOTHING is not yet determined (Example C [pdf
-- page 26]: "the Agencies would collect and analyze evidence to determine").
--   "direct": the text's reading is a reasonably proximate causal nexus (3.2 [pdf page 24]);
--   n.93 reports that one court of appeals has held "immediate consequence" instead, and says
--   the proximate cause standard is more consistent with the statute (fork F5).
--   "substantial": no minimum pecuniary threshold, no need to quantify (3.2 [pdf page 25]).
--   "reasonably foreseeable": an objective test (3.2 [pdf page 25]).
--   The last two fields are read for damages claims only (3.2 [pdf page 28]).
DECLARE `Effect of the conduct on U.S. commerce (3.2)` HAS
    `the commerce affected` IS A `Commerce an effect is on (3.2)`
    `the effect is proximately caused by the conduct` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the effect is substantial` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the effect is foreseeable to a reasonable person making practical business judgments` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the effect is an adverse one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the effect proximately caused the claimant's injury` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- 3.2 [pdf pages 28-29]: who brings the claim, which decides what "gives rise to" requires.
DECLARE `Kind of claim (3.2)` IS ONE OF
    `a civil action for equitable relief brought by the agencies`
    `a criminal enforcement action brought by the Department`
    `a damages action brought by a private plaintiff`
    `a damages action by the United States under Section 4A of the Clayton Act`

DECLARE `Claim (3.2)` HAS
    `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim (3.2)`
    `the claim is for injury to export business in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Section 6a's last sentence [pdf page 21]
    `the claimant's injury is a foreign injury` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.2 [pdf page 28]: read for a private damages claim only

-- 3 [pdf page 21]: the statute the agencies enforce.
DECLARE `Statute the agencies enforce (3)` IS ONE OF
    `the Sherman Act`
    `the FTC Act`
    `the Clayton Act`

-- n.100 [pdf page 29]: a victim of an offense reported by a leniency applicant.
DECLARE `Victim of an offense reported under the leniency policy (n.100)` HAS
    `the victim's antitrust injury is proximately caused by an adverse effect on trade or commerce within the United States, import trade or commerce, or the export trade or commerce of a person engaged in such trade or commerce in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that effect was proximately caused by the anticompetitive activity being reported` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 3.3 [pdf pages 29-30]: the form of U.S. government involvement in a transaction. The first
-- three are what the "requisite U.S. government involvement could include"; the fourth and
-- fifth are the two the text says do not sufficiently implicate U.S. government interests.
DECLARE `U.S. government involvement in a transaction (3.3)` IS ONE OF
    `an actual purchase of goods by the U.S. government for shipment abroad`
    `a U.S. government grant to a foreign government that is specifically earmarked for the transaction`
    `a U.S. government loan specifically earmarked for the transaction, on terms so generous that it amounts to a grant`
    `funding of the transaction merely by an international agency`
    `non-earmarked funds received by the foreign government from the United States as part of a general government-to-government aid program`
    `another form of U.S. government involvement`

DECLARE `Facts of U.S. government financing or purchasing (3.3)` HAS
    `the U.S. government is a purchaser, or substantially funds the purchase, of goods or services for consumption or use abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the involvement` IS A `U.S. government involvement in a transaction (3.3)`
    `as a result of its payment or financing, the U.S. government bears a substantial portion of the cost of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN   -- a finding
    `the effect of the conduct with respect to the sale of the goods or services falls primarily on U.S. taxpayers` IS A BOOLEAN   -- a finding

§§ `4.1 Comity`

-- 4.1 [pdf pages 30-32]: the matters the agencies weigh in the comity analysis, as facts the
-- caller states are present. "Among other things": the list is open, and "The relative
-- weight given to each factor depends on the facts and circumstances of each case", so the
-- encoding reports which are present and weighs nothing (fork F9).
DECLARE `Comity facts (4.1)` HAS
    `significant interests of a foreign sovereign would be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a purpose to affect, or an actual effect on, U.S. commerce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the effects of the conduct on the United States are significant and foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enforcement would conflict with a foreign jurisdiction's law or articulated policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the enforcement activities of another jurisdiction, including their remedies, may be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the objectives sought by U.S. enforcement could be achieved by foreign enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a foreign sovereign encourages or discourages the course of conduct, or leaves parties free to choose among courses of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.1 [pdf pages 31-32], n.144 [pdf page 42]: the foreign law said to conflict with U.S.
-- enforcement.
DECLARE `Foreign law and the conduct (4.1)` HAS
    `a person subject to the laws of both sovereigns can comply with both` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign law is neutral as to the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only foreign law said to conflict is a blocking statute, shown by nothing more than its existence` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `4.2 Foreign government involvement`

-- 4.2.1, n.112 [pdf page 33]: who the defendant is.
DECLARE `Kind of entity (4.2.1)` IS ONE OF
    `a foreign state itself`
    `a political subdivision of a foreign state`
    `another entity, which may be an agency or instrumentality of a foreign state`
    `an individual foreign official`

-- n.112 [pdf page 33]: the FSIA's definition of an "agency or instrumentality of a foreign
-- state", read for the third kind of entity only.
DECLARE `Entity before the FSIA (4.2.1)` HAS
    `the kind of entity` IS A `Kind of entity (4.2.1)`
    `it is a separate legal person, corporate or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an organ of a foreign state or political subdivision of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a majority of its shares or other ownership interest is owned by the foreign state itself or a political subdivision of it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Dole Food: the foreign state "itself" owns the majority
    `it is a citizen of a State of the United States, or created under the laws of a third country` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.2.1 [pdf pages 33-35], n.115: the action against the entity. "Commercial" is read by
-- the nature of the conduct, "rather than by reference to its purpose": the purpose field
-- is read by no rule. The three location fields are the three limbs of the commercial
-- activity exception, each "based upon" the particular conduct the action rests on.
DECLARE `Action against a foreign state (4.2.1)` HAS
    `the action is a civil case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the activity, the foreign state acts in the manner of a private player within a market, not as a regulator of it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- a finding: "the principal question"
    `the activity has a public or governmental purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is based upon the activity carried on in the United States by the foreign state, with substantial contact with the United States` IS A BOOLEAN   -- limb 1, n.115
    `the action is based upon an act performed in the United States in connection with the activity of the foreign state elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN   -- limb 2
    `the action is based upon an act outside the territory of the United States in connection with the activity of the foreign state elsewhere, and that act causes a direct effect in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN   -- limb 3

-- 4.2.2 [pdf pages 35-36]: what the foreign government did. The agencies' finding; a formal
-- representation may establish the command (see the next record).
DECLARE `Foreign government measure (4.2.2)` IS ONE OF
    `a command, refusal to comply with which would give rise to the imposition of penal or other severe sanctions`
    `a measure short of compulsion`
    `no measure of the foreign government`

-- 4.2.2 [pdf page 36], n.124 [pdf page 36].
DECLARE `Formal representation of compulsion (4.2.2)` HAS
    `the foreign government has formally represented that refusal to comply with its command would give rise to penal or other severe sanctions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the representation contains enough detail to enable the agencies to see precisely how the compulsion would be accomplished under foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is unsupported or ambiguous, or appears on its face to be internally inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.2.2 [pdf pages 36-37]: where the compelled conduct is accomplished.
DECLARE `Place of the compelled conduct (4.2.2)` IS ONE OF
    `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory`
    `in the United States`
    `not entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory, and not in the United States`

-- 4.2.2 [pdf pages 35-37], n.123 [pdf page 36]. The last two fields are facts the text says
-- do not by themselves bar the U.S. antitrust laws; no rule reads them.
DECLARE `Facts of foreign sovereign compulsion (4.2.2)` HAS
    `the measure` IS A `Foreign government measure (4.2.2)`
    `the conduct is discretionary` IS A BOOLEAN   -- n.123
    `the party can comply with both the foreign law and the U.S. antitrust laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `where the compelled conduct is accomplished` IS A `Place of the compelled conduct (4.2.2)`
    `the order comes from the foreign government acting in its governmental capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct would fall within the FSIA commercial activity exception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is lawful, approved, or encouraged in the foreign jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign jurisdiction has a strong policy in favor of the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.2.3 [pdf page 38]: who acted.
DECLARE `Actor of the conduct complained of (4.2.3)` IS ONE OF
    `the foreign sovereign`
    `an individual government official acting outside the official capacity`
    `a private actor`

-- 4.2.3 [pdf pages 38-39]. The approval field is read by no rule ("even when").
DECLARE `Facts of an act of state (4.2.3)` HAS
    `the actor` IS A `Actor of the conduct complained of (4.2.3)`
    `the specific conduct complained of is a public act of the sovereign` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was taken within the territorial jurisdiction of the sovereign` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct relates to a matter that is governmental, rather than commercial` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign government approved or condoned the acts` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.2.4 [pdf page 39].
DECLARE `Government entity petitioned (4.2.4)` IS ONE OF
    `a governmental entity in the United States`
    `a foreign government entity`

-- 4.2.4 [pdf page 39], n.136, n.137. "Genuine" is read as not a sham (fork F14). The intent
-- field is read by no rule ("even if the intent or effect of that effort is to restrain or
-- monopolize trade").
DECLARE `Facts of petitioning (4.2.4)` HAS
    `the government entity petitioned` IS A `Government entity petitioned (4.2.4)`
    `the conduct is an effort to obtain or influence action by the government entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the petitioning, ostensibly directed toward influencing governmental action, is a mere sham to cover an attempt to interfere directly with the business relationships of a competitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Noerr-Pennington would otherwise not apply` IS A BOOLEAN   -- n.137: a finding
    `the intent or effect of the effort is to restrain or monopolize trade` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `5 International cooperation`

-- 5 [pdf page 41], n.138 [pdf page 41]: where the investigations stand.
DECLARE `State of the investigations (5)` IS ONE OF
    `the Agency and the foreign authority are conducting parallel investigations of the matter`
    `the Agency or the foreign authority has closed its investigation, after they cooperated`
    `only one of them has an open investigation of the matter`

-- 5.1.1 [pdf pages 41-43]: documents or information the agencies seek. The location field is
-- read by no rule ("including documents or information located outside the United States").
DECLARE `Documents or information sought (5.1.1)` HAS
    `they are within the possession, custody, or control of an individual or entity subject to the jurisdiction of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are protected by the attorney-client privilege or the work-product doctrine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are located outside the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a foreign statute purports to prevent disclosing them for use in U.S. proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are sought by a Second Request in a transaction notified under the HSR Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.1.4 [pdf pages 47-48] and 5.2 [pdf pages 53-54]: the kinds of information the text
-- treats differently. n.160: publicly available information includes background on an
-- industry or company and public records such as court or securities filings. Agency
-- non-public information is information the agencies are not statutorily prohibited from
-- disclosing but normally treat as non-public (5.1.4).
DECLARE `Kind of information (5.1.4, 5.2)` IS ONE OF
    `relevant publicly available information`
    `agency non-public information`
    `confidential information submitted by a person`
    `matters occurring before the grand jury`
    `the identity of a leniency applicant, or information the applicant provided`

-- 5.1.4 [pdf pages 47-48], 5.2 [pdf page 54]: a waiver "limited in scope to a specific,
-- named matter" that designates the agencies that may share. Four states, since the text
-- treats a refusal apart from a waiver never asked for (fork F17).
DECLARE `Waiver of confidentiality (5.1.4)` IS ONE OF
    `the person has granted a waiver for this matter that designates the foreign authority`
    `the person has granted a waiver, but not for this matter or not designating the foreign authority`
    `the person has declined to provide a waiver`
    `no waiver has been requested or granted`

-- 5.1.4 [pdf pages 47-48], 2.6 [pdf page 13], 5.1.3 [pdf page 46]: an item the agencies
-- might give a foreign authority that is investigating the same transaction or conduct.
DECLARE `Information for a foreign authority (5.1.4)` HAS
    `the kind of information` IS A `Kind of information (5.1.4, 5.2)`
    `the foreign authority is also investigating the transaction or conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was submitted pursuant to the HSR Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waiver` IS A `Waiver of confidentiality (5.1.4)`
    `the agencies have reached an understanding that the foreign authority will maintain the information in confidence, consistent with its laws and rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an IAEAA mutual assistance agreement is in force between the United States and the foreign authority` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.1.4 [pdf page 48]: information the agencies might seek from, or have received from, a
-- foreign authority.
DECLARE `Information from a foreign authority (5.1.4)` HAS
    `it is privileged under U.S. law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agencies received it from the foreign authority pursuant to a waiver` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.2 [pdf page 53]: who would make the disclosure of a grand jury matter.
DECLARE `Person disclosing (5.2)` IS ONE OF
    `the Department`
    `a subject of the investigation, a grand jury witness, or a recipient of a grand jury subpoena`

-- 5.2 [pdf pages 53-54]: criminal-investigation information and a foreign authority.
DECLARE `Criminal investigation information for a foreign authority (5.2)` HAS
    `the kind of information` IS A `Kind of information (5.1.4, 5.2)`
    `the person disclosing` IS A `Person disclosing (5.2)`
    `an exception to the grand jury secrecy rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waiver` IS A `Waiver of confidentiality (5.1.4)`

-- 5.1.5 [pdf page 50]: a remedy that would include conduct or assets outside the United
-- States. Both are the Agency's findings.
DECLARE `Remedy reaching outside the United States (5.1.5)` HAS
    `including them is needed to effectively redress harm or threatened harm to U.S. commerce and consumers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `including them is consistent with the Agency's international comity analysis` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.2 [pdf page 53]: materials the Department requests of a leniency applicant. The location
-- field is read by no rule ("wherever located").
DECLARE `Materials requested of a leniency applicant (5.2)` HAS
    `they are in the applicant's possession, custody, or control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are located outside the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are requested by the Department in connection with the criminal antitrust investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are protected by the attorney-client privilege or the work-product doctrine` IS A BOOLEAN
